# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole #5: a MATCH-SCRUTINEE element binding
# read across a mutation of its collection inside the arm.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then
#   AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free ... in gorget_string_copy_cow
# The `case Some(x)` binding aliases the element in place, and the arm's pushes
# realloc the backing store out from under it.
#
# INTENDED: ACCEPT, run ASan-clean, and print the PRE-MUTATION value
# ("alpha-heap-forced-payload").
#
# ⚠ NOTE THE POLARITY — this hole's answer is NOT a reject, unlike its siblings.
# Owner-ruled (recorded in TODO.md): this is the TEMPORAL axis — a
# `CowBorrowMutation` MATERIALIZE, the same axis as the intra-function CoW sever
# pinned by `sound_getchain_sever_accept.gg` — and NOT the call-arg D10(b)
# place-overlap reject axis. The mutation site is VISIBLE here, so the clone can
# be placed lazily at the binding; the reject axis exists only where the
# mutation hides behind a call boundary and the sole rescue would be a
# speculative unconditional clone. The ruling is explicit that this must be kept
# OUT of the place-overlap chokepoint.
#
# So a chokepoint rebuild that "fixes" this fixture by rejecting the program has
# implemented the wrong ruling, and this fixture will still be red — correctly.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): OUT OF SUBSET — "method `.first()` is
